 "notes": [
  "On 1h, price crossing up through the London previous high gave 1,105 entries in 890 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.09% ahead of random entries, inside a band of -0.25% to 0.25%. The New York version landed at -0.01%. The cross up through the previous day's high fires a bit more than twice as often as the London one and also stayed inside the band, at 0.13%.",
  "On 4h, being long while price stayed above the previous day's high gave 5,623 entries in 685 moves. They were 0.51% ahead of random entries after 20 candles, above a band that tops out at 0.36%. The gap holds without its strongest stretch, between Aug 10 and Sep 9, 2021, and shows at 10 and 100 candles, but not at 50. On 1h the same condition was 0.12% ahead, inside the band.",
  "The 4h result does not hold on any one pair. On SOL it was 0.97% ahead, but only because of the run between Aug 10 and Sep 9, 2021. On BTC it was 0.43% ahead, and that depends on signals between Dec 25, 2020 and Jan 8, 2021. ETH was 0.1% ahead, inside the band. On daily candles the condition has 28 moves, under the minimum of 30, so it is not judged.",
  "Price crossing down through the London previous low on 4h was 0.75% behind random entries, just past the band's lower edge of -0.7%. Two entries on Apr 10–12, 2024 explain it, and without them the result is chance. It stays worse at 50 and 100 candles, but no single pair is outside its own band. On 1h the same cross was -0.14%, inside the band.",
  "Two other results come from a single stretch. On BTC 1h, the cross up through the previous day's high was 0.2% ahead, but six entries on Jan 5–7, 2021 carry it. On SOL 4h, staying above the London previous midpoint was 0.38% ahead, but this depends on signals between Jul 21, 2021 and Sep 9, 2021, and it is chance at every other horizon.",
  "For a long DCA bot, session-level breaks add no timing on these pairs, so the DCA orders and take profit do the work. Holding above the previous day's high on 4h is the one condition worth testing as a filter beside your other start conditions. It holds on about four and a half times as many candles as the cross over that high, so it narrows entries without pinning them to one candle. It showed nothing on ETH alone, so check it on your own pair first."
